{{also|Disciple}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang}} ''[[discipul]]'', from {{etyl|la}} {{term|discipulus||a pupil, learner}} < {{term|discere||to learn}}; akin to {{term|docere||to teach}}. Later influenced or superceded in Middle English by {{etyl|fro}} ''[[deciple]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/dɪˈsaɪpəl/}}
* {{audio|En-us-disciple.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who learns from another, especially one who then teaches others.
# An active [[follower]] or [[adherent]] of someone, or some [[philosophy]] etc.

====Related terms====
* [[discipleship]]
* [[discipline]]

